WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:03.010
- So Sidney Powell has
filed a Motion to Dismiss

00:00:03.010 --> 00:00:06.820
the multi-billion dollar
lawsuit filed by Dominion.

00:00:06.820 --> 00:00:08.660
And yes, the headlines are true.

00:00:08.660 --> 00:00:11.700
Her principal defense in
this Motion to Dismiss

00:00:11.700 --> 00:00:14.290
is that no reasonable person
would listen to the things

00:00:14.290 --> 00:00:17.900
that she said and understand it as a fact.

00:00:17.900 --> 00:00:20.700
Now, that is both true and hilarious,

00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:23.380
but probably not hilarious for the reasons

00:00:23.380 --> 00:00:26.290
that most pundits have discussed.

00:00:26.290 --> 00:00:27.360
But we'll get to that

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:30.989
because this whole motion is ridiculous.

00:00:30.989 --> 00:00:33.656
(upbeat music)

00:00:35.070 --> 00:00:38.240
So welcome back to Kraken Watch 2021.

00:00:38.240 --> 00:00:42.210
And today we have Sydney
Powell's attempt to get out

00:00:42.210 --> 00:00:45.040
of the multi-billion dollar
lawsuit that Dominion filed.

00:00:45.040 --> 00:00:46.430
To bring you up to speed,

00:00:46.430 --> 00:00:49.820
Dominion claims that Sidney
Powell said all number

00:00:49.820 --> 00:00:51.560
of crazy things during the election.

00:00:51.560 --> 00:00:54.830
And as a result, they lost
a huge amount of money,

00:00:54.830 --> 00:00:58.480
and as a result they have sued
Sidney Powell for defamation.

00:00:58.480 --> 00:00:59.800
So first off, where are we?

00:00:59.800 --> 00:01:01.650
Well, this is a Motion to Dismiss.

00:01:01.650 --> 00:01:03.940
So if you are a defendant in a case,

00:01:03.940 --> 00:01:07.470
you can claim that the plaintiff's
case is legally deficient

00:01:07.470 --> 00:01:09.410
by filing what's called
a Motion to Dismiss.

00:01:09.410 --> 00:01:12.300
You ask the court to dismiss the case.

00:01:12.300 --> 00:01:14.160
Now, contrary to popular belief,

00:01:14.160 --> 00:01:15.910
as we've talked about
a lot on this channel,

00:01:15.910 --> 00:01:18.490
a Motion to Dismiss doesn't
present any evidence.

00:01:18.490 --> 00:01:20.600
All you're doing is saying that

00:01:20.600 --> 00:01:22.520
for the purposes of this motion,

00:01:22.520 --> 00:01:24.820
everything that the plaintiff claims

00:01:24.820 --> 00:01:27.930
in their complaint is understood as true.

00:01:27.930 --> 00:01:29.120
They're not conceding that,

00:01:29.120 --> 00:01:30.180
but they're saying look,

00:01:30.180 --> 00:01:31.560
we're not going to dispute the facts

00:01:31.560 --> 00:01:32.710
at this particular juncture.

00:01:32.710 --> 00:01:33.960
We're just going to
assume that that's true.

00:01:33.960 --> 00:01:36.310
And even assuming that everything is true

00:01:36.310 --> 00:01:37.980
and looking at the allegations

00:01:37.980 --> 00:01:40.260
of the light most
favorable to the plaintiff,

00:01:40.260 --> 00:01:42.830
it still fails right out of the gate.

00:01:42.830 --> 00:01:44.570
Now, this is a very common tactic.

00:01:44.570 --> 00:01:46.710
There are later motions that you can make

00:01:46.710 --> 00:01:48.500
that will incorporate evidence.

00:01:48.500 --> 00:01:51.160
But the idea is to try and get
rid of the case immediately

00:01:51.160 --> 00:01:53.190
before going through
very expensive discovery

00:01:53.190 --> 00:01:55.160
that will gather all of that evidence.

00:01:55.160 --> 00:01:57.510
Now, in addition to trying to
just dismiss the case outright

00:01:57.510 --> 00:01:59.280
they're also moving for a
whole bunch of other things,

00:01:59.280 --> 00:02:02.810
like moving the venue from
Washington D.C to Texas

00:02:02.810 --> 00:02:04.680
and a bunch of other things
that we're not gonna get into

00:02:04.680 --> 00:02:06.450
because the real heart of this motion

00:02:06.450 --> 00:02:08.960
is trying to dismiss it from the court

00:02:08.960 --> 00:02:11.150
and not having to deal
with it anymore at all.

00:02:11.150 --> 00:02:13.310
And a quick reminder, defamation is a tort

00:02:13.310 --> 00:02:15.970
where you claim that someone
said something factual

00:02:15.970 --> 00:02:17.850
about you that is untrue

00:02:17.850 --> 00:02:21.250
and that caused damages to
you and your reputations.

00:02:21.250 --> 00:02:23.460
Of course, that requires
that the things being said

00:02:23.460 --> 00:02:26.480
are factual, being capable of verification

00:02:26.480 --> 00:02:28.480
and are not someone's opinion.

00:02:28.480 --> 00:02:30.710
It's not hyperbole, it's not parody.

00:02:30.710 --> 00:02:33.540
And so you can imagine that
a lot of the suit hinges

00:02:33.540 --> 00:02:36.200
on the nature of the
statements at issue here.

00:02:36.200 --> 00:02:37.060
And right off the bat,

00:02:37.060 --> 00:02:39.240
Sidney Powell and her attorneys
trying and argue some things

00:02:39.240 --> 00:02:40.790
to tip things in their favor.

00:02:40.790 --> 00:02:42.710
The first argument is that of course,

00:02:42.710 --> 00:02:45.580
this whole affair
involved political speech,

00:02:45.580 --> 00:02:47.580
an election, a president being elected,

00:02:47.580 --> 00:02:50.650
a fiercely contested
election in a pandemic.

00:02:50.650 --> 00:02:51.530
And as you can imagine,

00:02:51.530 --> 00:02:53.530
free speech rights are at
their absolute pinnacle

00:02:53.530 --> 00:02:55.850
when you're talking
about political speech.

00:02:55.850 --> 00:02:58.030
So if the court were to err on one side,

00:02:58.030 --> 00:03:00.010
it should be allowing more political

00:03:00.010 --> 00:03:03.030
or arguably political
speech than stifling it.

00:03:03.030 --> 00:03:06.360
And then number two is that
Dominion is a public figure.

00:03:06.360 --> 00:03:08.180
And if Dominion is a public figure,

00:03:08.180 --> 00:03:10.770
they're subject to a
much higher requirement

00:03:10.770 --> 00:03:12.100
to be able to prove defamation.

00:03:12.100 --> 00:03:14.020
This is the Actual Malice standard

00:03:14.020 --> 00:03:15.380
that a lot of people have talked about

00:03:15.380 --> 00:03:16.690
in a defamation context.

00:03:16.690 --> 00:03:18.210
And I don't wanna beat a dead horse here,

00:03:18.210 --> 00:03:21.510
but I will say this every time
we talk about defamation law.

00:03:21.510 --> 00:03:24.000
Actual Malice doesn't mean
that you said a statement

00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:25.210
because you hated someone.

00:03:25.210 --> 00:03:28.380
Actual Malice means that
you said a statement

00:03:28.380 --> 00:03:30.170
that was false knowing it was false

00:03:30.170 --> 00:03:32.760
or operating in a reckless disregard

00:03:32.760 --> 00:03:34.700
for whether it was true or not.

00:03:34.700 --> 00:03:36.130
And if Dominion is a public figure

00:03:36.130 --> 00:03:37.970
or a limited purpose public figure

00:03:37.970 --> 00:03:40.310
with respect to election-related things,

00:03:40.310 --> 00:03:41.960
then it would have to prove

00:03:41.960 --> 00:03:45.860
that Sidney Powell said these
statements with Actual Malice,

00:03:45.860 --> 00:03:47.110
which is a pretty high burden.

00:03:47.110 --> 00:03:49.500
And fair enough as we
covered on this very channel,

00:03:49.500 --> 00:03:51.130
Sidney Powell might be right about this

00:03:51.130 --> 00:03:53.450
and Dominion faces an
uphill battle to be able

00:03:53.450 --> 00:03:56.450
to prove the allegations
that they included

00:03:56.450 --> 00:03:57.450
in their complaint.

00:03:57.450 --> 00:04:00.530
But that's where this
Motion to Dismiss starts

00:04:00.530 --> 00:04:01.960
to go off the rails.

00:04:01.960 --> 00:04:05.550
Because now Sidney Powell
starts arguing substantively

00:04:05.550 --> 00:04:07.340
that these statements that she made,

00:04:07.340 --> 00:04:10.870
the hundreds of them cannot
give rise to defamation

00:04:10.870 --> 00:04:14.430
and here's where things get
a little bit ridiculous.

00:04:14.430 --> 00:04:15.940
And then Sydney Powell goes straight

00:04:15.940 --> 00:04:17.667
to the heart of it and argues.

00:04:17.667 --> 00:04:18.920
"Analyzed under these facts,

00:04:18.920 --> 00:04:20.280
even assuming arguendo,

00:04:20.280 --> 00:04:22.010
that each of the statements
alleged in the complaint

00:04:22.010 --> 00:04:23.750
could be proved true or false,

00:04:23.750 --> 00:04:25.900
no reasonable person would conclude

00:04:25.900 --> 00:04:29.100
that the statements were
truly statements of fact."

00:04:29.100 --> 00:04:31.610
And there are lots of
people on the internet

00:04:31.610 --> 00:04:33.770
taking that statement and
saying that Sidney Powell

00:04:33.770 --> 00:04:35.500
has admitted that everything that she said

00:04:35.500 --> 00:04:39.840
was completely false and
admits that she's a liar.

00:04:39.840 --> 00:04:41.720
Not so fast though.

00:04:41.720 --> 00:04:43.970
The things that she's
arguing are pretty crazy,

00:04:43.970 --> 00:04:45.410
that's not one of them.

00:04:45.410 --> 00:04:47.890
That is technically a
defense to defamation.

00:04:47.890 --> 00:04:49.870
to say that the things that you're saying

00:04:49.870 --> 00:04:51.724
are not statements of fact.

00:04:51.724 --> 00:04:54.610
What she's hearkening back to is the idea

00:04:54.610 --> 00:04:56.770
that what she is saying is opinion.

00:04:56.770 --> 00:04:58.580
There are lots of facts out there

00:04:58.580 --> 00:05:00.180
and then she just interprets them.

00:05:00.180 --> 00:05:02.580
And that interpretation
is not a statement of fact

00:05:02.580 --> 00:05:04.930
that can give rise to defamation.

00:05:04.930 --> 00:05:06.880
This is not a bad strategy.

00:05:06.880 --> 00:05:08.350
It is a bit of a mea culpa.

00:05:08.350 --> 00:05:10.500
It's not a good strategy,

00:05:10.500 --> 00:05:12.180
but it's probably the best strategy

00:05:12.180 --> 00:05:14.100
that she has in this context.

00:05:14.100 --> 00:05:15.570
And it's not a straight up admission

00:05:15.570 --> 00:05:17.360
that everything she says was false.

00:05:17.360 --> 00:05:18.980
In fact, later in the motion,

00:05:18.980 --> 00:05:20.610
they say that Sidney Powell actually

00:05:20.610 --> 00:05:22.410
does believe these things.

00:05:22.410 --> 00:05:23.540
They are sort of arguing

00:05:23.540 --> 00:05:25.870
that no reasonable person
would believe them,

00:05:25.870 --> 00:05:28.230
but also that she does believe them.

00:05:28.230 --> 00:05:31.170
But we'll get to that in a
second because it's just crazy.

00:05:31.170 --> 00:05:33.050
The other thing that
she's sort of arguing here

00:05:33.050 --> 00:05:36.180
is the idea that you
can sometimes say things

00:05:36.180 --> 00:05:39.050
that would give rise to
defamation as a fact,

00:05:39.050 --> 00:05:42.260
but given the context of the situation,

00:05:42.260 --> 00:05:43.580
it sort of walks it back.

00:05:43.580 --> 00:05:46.370
And the famous example of this
is the fake letter written

00:05:46.370 --> 00:05:48.860
by Jerry Falwell that
appeared in Hustler Magazine.

00:05:48.860 --> 00:05:52.380
Where this putative Jerry
Falwell talked about losing

00:05:52.380 --> 00:05:54.690
his virginity and all
kinds of raunchy things

00:05:54.690 --> 00:05:55.770
in Hustler Magazine.

00:05:55.770 --> 00:05:58.540
It was clearly satire and parody.

00:05:58.540 --> 00:06:00.140
And even though these were things

00:06:00.140 --> 00:06:02.120
that were sort of alleged as being true,

00:06:02.120 --> 00:06:03.880
these were factual statements.

00:06:03.880 --> 00:06:07.090
The context made it clear that
no one would understand these

00:06:07.090 --> 00:06:10.110
to be actual allegations
about Jerry Falwell.

00:06:10.110 --> 00:06:12.810
Now ironically, the
context may not actually

00:06:12.810 --> 00:06:14.620
help Sidney Powell in this case.

00:06:14.620 --> 00:06:17.200
Because not only is she
saying all of these things

00:06:17.200 --> 00:06:20.050
on TV, on Fox News, at the RNC,

00:06:20.050 --> 00:06:22.870
where she argues that it's
clearly just political theater,

00:06:22.870 --> 00:06:25.410
but she's also making
these exact same arguments

00:06:25.410 --> 00:06:27.550
in front of judges.

00:06:27.550 --> 00:06:29.980
She filed numerous lawsuits contending

00:06:29.980 --> 00:06:32.250
that these things were actual facts.

00:06:32.250 --> 00:06:34.320
So Sidney Powell finds
herself on the horns

00:06:34.320 --> 00:06:35.310
of a dilemma here.

00:06:35.310 --> 00:06:36.230
Because on the one hand,

00:06:36.230 --> 00:06:38.400
she's arguing these
aren't factual statements.

00:06:38.400 --> 00:06:41.540
They're more akin to an
interpretation or an opinion,

00:06:41.540 --> 00:06:43.740
especially given the context.

00:06:43.740 --> 00:06:44.990
But then on the other,

00:06:44.990 --> 00:06:47.720
she's actually making
these arguments to judges.

00:06:47.720 --> 00:06:50.480
She wanted the courts
to actually intervene

00:06:50.480 --> 00:06:53.260
and grant temporary restraining orders,

00:06:53.260 --> 00:06:55.400
preliminary injunctions, relief,

00:06:55.400 --> 00:06:58.220
to overturn the elections
on the basis of the things

00:06:58.220 --> 00:06:59.430
that she's saying here.

00:06:59.430 --> 00:07:01.810
There might be ways to thread this needle

00:07:01.810 --> 00:07:03.220
but this ain't it chief.

00:07:03.220 --> 00:07:06.520
Now, unfortunately there
are some practical reasons

00:07:06.520 --> 00:07:08.460
why a lawyer might dissemble

00:07:08.460 --> 00:07:11.780
or at least say different
things in different contexts

00:07:11.780 --> 00:07:14.730
and that's that it's really
hard to sanction a lawyer.

00:07:14.730 --> 00:07:16.310
Judges hate sanctioning lawyers.

00:07:16.310 --> 00:07:19.160
Bar associations hate sanctioning lawyers.

00:07:19.160 --> 00:07:23.040
So if you're going to
claim that the things

00:07:23.040 --> 00:07:25.780
that you were saying
were complete nonsense,

00:07:25.780 --> 00:07:28.650
better to say that in
defense of a defamation case

00:07:28.650 --> 00:07:32.120
where you have millions
of dollars at stake

00:07:32.120 --> 00:07:34.690
and just try and roll the dice

00:07:34.690 --> 00:07:36.860
with respect to being
sanctioned by the courts

00:07:36.860 --> 00:07:37.693
that you're appearing in.

00:07:37.693 --> 00:07:39.020
Now, the irony here is that

00:07:39.020 --> 00:07:42.290
there are pending sanctions
motions against Sidney Powell

00:07:42.290 --> 00:07:45.870
and the things that she is
arguing in this briefing

00:07:45.870 --> 00:07:49.270
may hurt her in those sanctions context.

00:07:49.270 --> 00:07:51.950
Now, the dollar amounts are
not going to be the same

00:07:51.950 --> 00:07:55.660
but potentially theoretically
her Bar license might be

00:07:55.660 --> 00:07:57.690
at issue in some of these cases.

00:07:57.690 --> 00:07:59.080
Though, I wouldn't hold my breath

00:07:59.080 --> 00:08:01.640
because judges hate to sanction lawyers,

00:08:01.640 --> 00:08:03.550
just like lawyers hate
to sanction lawyers.

00:08:03.550 --> 00:08:06.630
Though, at the same time it is
baked right into legal ethics

00:08:06.630 --> 00:08:09.740
that you cannot knowingly lie or dissemble

00:08:09.740 --> 00:08:11.920
to a judge or tribunal.

00:08:11.920 --> 00:08:14.330
It's all over the ethical rules

00:08:14.330 --> 00:08:16.530
for lawyers in every single state.

00:08:16.530 --> 00:08:20.080
And she's running a really,
really fine line here.

00:08:20.080 --> 00:08:22.520
And I would not wanna be in her position.

00:08:22.520 --> 00:08:23.353
And on the one hand,

00:08:23.353 --> 00:08:24.550
she's arguing that no reasonable person

00:08:24.550 --> 00:08:26.440
would believe any of these things.

00:08:26.440 --> 00:08:29.020
And yet she made these arguments to judges

00:08:29.020 --> 00:08:31.910
and tried to argue them in front of juries

00:08:31.910 --> 00:08:33.750
in a way to get them to
believe these things.

00:08:33.750 --> 00:08:37.240
And of course, we know that
a lot of people believed

00:08:37.240 --> 00:08:38.330
the things that she was saying.

00:08:38.330 --> 00:08:41.020
There were thousands of
people in Washington D.C

00:08:41.020 --> 00:08:42.960
who stormed the Capitol.

00:08:42.960 --> 00:08:45.270
I was here, I can attest to it.

00:08:45.270 --> 00:08:47.530
And so hard to say

00:08:47.530 --> 00:08:49.270
that no reasonable person would believe it

00:08:49.270 --> 00:08:51.300
because a lot of people believed it.

00:08:51.300 --> 00:08:52.540
Now, of course, query whether the people

00:08:52.540 --> 00:08:54.820
that stormed the capital were
reasonable people or not,

00:08:54.820 --> 00:08:55.930
that's not the way

00:08:55.930 --> 00:08:57.990
that the reasonable person standard works.

00:08:57.990 --> 00:09:00.600
But still, it's probably
pretty good evidence

00:09:00.600 --> 00:09:03.920
that people believed what
she was saying enough

00:09:03.920 --> 00:09:04.900
to act on it.

00:09:04.900 --> 00:09:06.400
And I wouldn't wanna be in her position

00:09:06.400 --> 00:09:07.900
and trying to walk that back and saying

00:09:07.900 --> 00:09:09.870
it was so ridiculous and non-factual

00:09:09.870 --> 00:09:11.430
that no one would believe it.

00:09:11.430 --> 00:09:14.020
But look, she has grifted
a whole lot of people

00:09:14.020 --> 00:09:15.350
out of a whole lot of money

00:09:15.350 --> 00:09:16.677
by saying dumber things than that.

00:09:16.677 --> 00:09:20.880
- The Dominion operators
went in and injected votes

00:09:20.880 --> 00:09:22.240
and changed the whole system.

00:09:22.240 --> 00:09:23.680
- And perhaps the biggest irony here

00:09:23.680 --> 00:09:26.390
is that she's arguing that as an attorney,

00:09:26.390 --> 00:09:29.410
as an advocate, as a zealous
advocate in front of a court

00:09:29.410 --> 00:09:32.310
you have to do what's
right by your client.

00:09:32.310 --> 00:09:35.520
But that cannot mean that
you can just make stuff up

00:09:35.520 --> 00:09:37.089
and fabricate arguments,

00:09:37.089 --> 00:09:39.520
that's not the way legal ethics work.

00:09:39.520 --> 00:09:41.210
And it's at this point in the brief

00:09:41.210 --> 00:09:43.060
where basically Powell's legal team

00:09:43.060 --> 00:09:45.510
stops citing actual legal authority

00:09:45.510 --> 00:09:47.480
and they start just citing websites.

00:09:47.480 --> 00:09:49.450
Now, that's really bad for two reasons.

00:09:49.450 --> 00:09:51.450
Number one, a Motion
to Dismiss is all about

00:09:51.450 --> 00:09:53.090
the law itself for the most part

00:09:53.090 --> 00:09:56.050
and you can't really bring in new evidence

00:09:56.050 --> 00:09:58.920
even if it's not necessarily controverted.

00:09:58.920 --> 00:10:01.710
So trying to bring in these
external websites talking

00:10:01.710 --> 00:10:04.940
about the robust public
discussion, not a good look.

00:10:04.940 --> 00:10:06.610
And it's almost certain that the court

00:10:06.610 --> 00:10:10.170
will bounce this motion
on that basis alone,

00:10:10.170 --> 00:10:12.380
which takes us to the
arguments about Actual Malice.

00:10:12.380 --> 00:10:14.890
And recall the Actual
Malice is a high standard.

00:10:14.890 --> 00:10:18.390
And it all hinges on what the
alleged defamer was thinking.

00:10:18.390 --> 00:10:21.140
Did they know the things that
they were saying were false?

00:10:21.140 --> 00:10:23.430
Did they know or should they have known?

00:10:23.430 --> 00:10:25.210
Were they reckless with respect to whether

00:10:25.210 --> 00:10:26.750
it was true or false.

00:10:26.750 --> 00:10:29.370
And Sidney Powell tries to get around that

00:10:29.370 --> 00:10:31.780
and get this case dismissed on the basis

00:10:31.780 --> 00:10:33.850
that she had a true belief that the things

00:10:33.850 --> 00:10:37.910
that she was saying were true and factual.

00:10:37.910 --> 00:10:40.680
And so she's arguing that
she couldn't possibly

00:10:40.680 --> 00:10:42.270
have had actual malice with respect

00:10:42.270 --> 00:10:43.970
to these are false statements

00:10:43.970 --> 00:10:45.060
because she really believed them.

00:10:45.060 --> 00:10:48.670
So yes, she is arguing
that no reasonable person

00:10:48.670 --> 00:10:50.830
would believe that these
were factual statements.

00:10:50.830 --> 00:10:53.580
And at the same time, she
is arguing that she did

00:10:53.580 --> 00:10:56.010
actually believe the
things that she was saying

00:10:57.260 --> 00:10:58.190
It's crazy.

00:10:58.190 --> 00:11:00.550
- President Trump won by a landslide,

00:11:00.550 --> 00:11:02.290
we are going to prove it.

00:11:02.290 --> 00:11:04.930
And we are gonna reclaim
the United States of America

00:11:04.930 --> 00:11:07.690
for the people who vote for freedom.

00:11:07.690 --> 00:11:09.090
- Then as we round out this motion,

00:11:09.090 --> 00:11:11.470
we get to another argument to dismiss

00:11:11.470 --> 00:11:14.500
a co-defendant called DTR,
Defending the Republic.

00:11:14.500 --> 00:11:16.630
And in something that
I think is just funny

00:11:16.630 --> 00:11:18.140
as a practicing lawyer,

00:11:18.140 --> 00:11:21.050
you'll notice that there are
some formatting errors here.

00:11:21.050 --> 00:11:24.230
The font has changed colors,
sometimes it changes back.

00:11:24.230 --> 00:11:28.630
What that is indicative of is
when lawyers copy and paste

00:11:28.630 --> 00:11:31.180
from another brief and then forgets

00:11:31.180 --> 00:11:34.570
that sometimes external documents
are in a different color.

00:11:34.570 --> 00:11:36.490
Often it's dark blue.

00:11:36.490 --> 00:11:40.380
And so that's almost always
why a different section

00:11:40.380 --> 00:11:42.340
has a different font color

00:11:42.340 --> 00:11:43.590
and appears a little bit lighter,

00:11:43.590 --> 00:11:46.590
and it varies depending on the sentence.

00:11:46.590 --> 00:11:48.220
It's because they did a really sloppy job

00:11:48.220 --> 00:11:49.120
of copying and pasting.

00:11:49.120 --> 00:11:51.600
Now, copying and pasting
isn't the end of the world.

00:11:51.600 --> 00:11:53.460
Lawyers are allowed to do that,

00:11:53.460 --> 00:11:56.550
you shouldn't necessarily
reinvent the wheel.

00:11:56.550 --> 00:11:59.710
But it's a real bad look
when it's very clear

00:11:59.710 --> 00:12:02.010
that you're copying from some other brief

00:12:02.010 --> 00:12:04.240
and not even bothering
to change the formatting.

00:12:04.240 --> 00:12:05.930
So this motion is risible,

00:12:05.930 --> 00:12:09.580
the court is almost certainly
going to deny this motion.

00:12:09.580 --> 00:12:11.300
There's a better version of this motion

00:12:11.300 --> 00:12:12.840
that could have been made.

00:12:12.840 --> 00:12:16.030
But you play the hand that
you're dealt, I suppose.

00:12:16.030 --> 00:12:18.160
And a lot of people are dog piling

00:12:18.160 --> 00:12:20.190
on this saying that Sydney Powell admitted

00:12:20.190 --> 00:12:21.230
that she was a liar.

00:12:21.230 --> 00:12:22.850
It doesn't go that far.

00:12:22.850 --> 00:12:25.580
She does argue extremely
contradictory things

00:12:25.580 --> 00:12:26.850
that are going to hurt her case.

00:12:26.850 --> 00:12:28.870
It's going to hurt her in other contexts

00:12:28.870 --> 00:12:31.600
where she might have
to deal with sanctions.

00:12:31.600 --> 00:12:35.100
But we don't need to make
up additional reasons

00:12:35.100 --> 00:12:39.160
for why this is a bad
look and why she's crazy

00:12:39.160 --> 00:12:41.330
because she's crazy enough on her own.

00:12:41.330 --> 00:12:43.550
But what do you think, do
you agree with my analysis?

00:12:43.550 --> 00:12:44.830
Leave your objections in the comments

00:12:44.830 --> 00:12:45.830
and check out this playlist over here

00:12:45.830 --> 00:12:47.390
with all my other real law reviews,

00:12:47.390 --> 00:12:49.960
where I have talked about
Kraken Law ad nauseum.

00:12:49.960 --> 00:12:53.203
So check out these other videos
and I will see you in court.

